{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>A solemn rest, a remembrance of teru'ah</b> — on Shabbat one does not blow, for shofar-blowing does not override Shabbat, and it has only זכרון תרועה, but in the Temple one blows. תקעו שופר בציון — rashei tevot: שבת שבציון תוקעין — even on Shabbat." "<b>זכרון</b> — three times in the Masorah: דין, and the other: אין זכרון לראשונים, and the other: אין זכרון לחכם עם הכסיל. Corresponding to three books opened on Rosh HaShanah. Therefore in the two [verses] it is written אין זכרון — these are the righteous and the wicked, who do not need to be remembered further, but these are sealed immediately for life and these for death. And that is אין זכרון לחכם, and also in the second verse it is written אין זכרון, which corresponds to the wicked. But in the third verse it is written זכרון, which corresponds to the intermediate ones, who are suspended and standing, and need to be remembered further on Yom HaKippurim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:25.176162760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}